---
// The page a visitor lands on after following a link that no longer resolves — an old post
// URL, a renamed project, a typo. Built as dist/404.html; the web server has to be told to
// serve it (nginx: `error_page 404 /404.html;`), otherwise it stays an unreachable file.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
---
<Page
  title="Page Not Found"
  url="/404.html"
  description="This page does not exist. Try the blog, the publications, or the projects instead."
>
<p>
  There is nothing at this address. It may have moved, or the link that brought you here may
  have a typo in it.
</p>

<p>
  Try one of these instead:
</p>

<ul>
  <li><a href="/">the homepage</a></li>
  <li><a href="/blog/">the blog</a></li>
  <li><a href="/publications/">the publications</a></li>
  <li><a href="/projects/">the projects</a></li>
</ul>

<p>
  If you followed a link from somewhere on this site, <a href="/contact/">let me know</a> and
  I will fix it.
</p>
</Page>
